course: dictionary
lesson: 521
title: The Assyrians
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Assyrian is a word you will meet in history lessons and in the Bible. Look at the clues around it: «The Assyrians built a strong, feared empire with great palaces at Nineveh.» Empire and palaces tell you that Assyrian is about a powerful kingdom of long ago.
explain: Assyrian can work in different ways. It can describe something, as in «Assyrian palaces». It can name a person, as in «an Assyrian», or a language. Ask yourself: is the word describing something, or naming someone? The words around it will tell you which.
explain: «Babylon grew into a famous city, the Assyrians ruled from great palaces, and finally the Persians built the largest empire the world had yet seen.» Here the Assyrians sit in a list of empires, so they are a people who ruled long ago. Try your meaning in the sentence and check it still makes sense.
fact: Assyria was a powerful empire in Mesopotamia, in what is mostly northern Iraq today.
fact: Its great cities included Nineveh and Assur, and it was strongest from about 900 to 600 BC.
fact: «The Assyrian king Ashurbanipal collected a huge library of clay tablets.» Baked clay does not rot or burn away easily, so many tablets survive.
fact: Assyrians today are a people of the Middle East and around the world, mostly Christians, who speak Neo-Aramaic, also called Assyrian or Syriac.
fact: In the Bible, the Assyrians conquered the northern Kingdom of Israel, and Jonah was sent to preach in their city Nineveh.
exercise: In «Assyrian palaces», what kind of word is Assyrian? | *An adjective, describing the palaces | A place name | A verb showing action | A noun for a person
exercise: Assyria was a powerful empire in which region? | *Mesopotamia | Australia | Scotland | Antarctica
exercise: In the Bible, Jonah was sent to preach in which city? | *Nineveh | London | Rome | Babylon
test: Why have so many Assyrian clay tablets survived? | *Baked clay does not rot or burn away easily | They were made of gold | They were written only on paper
test: Which language do many Assyrians today speak? | Ancient Greek | French | *Neo-Aramaic, also called Assyrian or Syriac | Mandarin
exam: Which statement is true? | Nineveh was a town in London | *Assyria was a powerful empire in Mesopotamia | Assyria was a small village in Scotland | Assyrians spoke only Greek
